INT. DEEP-SPACE MINING BARGE - CONTROL ROOM - CONTINUOUS

Steel. Screens. Asteroid dust drifting past the viewport.

CAPTAIN RUTH ESCOBAR-LINDGREN (50s, scarred cheek, gray crewcut). Hands on the console.

First Mate JUBAL TIDWELL (30s, headset, nervous). Eyes on the scanner.

ENGINEER PRIYAMVADA "PRI" NAGARAJAN (40s, goggles pushed up). Wrench in her fist.

Cadet WREN MALLORY (teen, oversized helmet). Wide-eyed.

                    RUTH
          Jubal. Status.

                    JUBAL
          Hull at sixty percent, Captain.

                    RUTH
          Pri. Engines.

                    PRI
          Coughing. But alive, Ruth.

                    RUTH
          Wren. Stay low.

                    WREN
          Yes, Captain.

A rumble. The deck shudders. Dust sifts from the ceiling.

                    JUBAL
          Another impact. Starboard.

                    PRI
          Jubal, that's the third this hour.

                    RUTH
          Pri, patch it.

                    PRI
          With what? Spit?

                    RUTH
          With whatever you've got.

Pri sighs, swings her goggles down, and heads for the hatch. Wren scrambles after her.

                    WREN
          Pri, can I help?

                    PRI
          Hold the light, kid.

The hatch seals behind them. Ruth and Jubal watch the scanner. A red dot creeps closer.

                    JUBAL
          Captain, it's matching our speed.

                    RUTH
          I see it.

                    JUBAL
          What do we do?

                    RUTH
          We wait.
